course: dictionary
lesson: 7550
title: Two words that look alike
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Some words look almost the same but mean very different things. Preform and perform are one such pair. Read the words around the word to find the right meaning: «A plastic bottle is blown from a preform, a small finger-sized plastic tube.» A tube and a mould are objects, so preform must be a thing, not an action.
explain: Perform means to do something for an audience, like a play or a song. Preform, as a noun, means an object that has been partly shaped before its final shape. The clues show this: the preform is heated and blown up with air inside a bottle-shaped mould.
explain: Preform can also be a rare verb meaning to shape something beforehand. You will mostly see it in technical writing. If a story about a school show uses preform, it is probably a spelling mistake for perform. Swap in your meaning and check that the sentence still makes sense.
fact: A preform is an object that has been partly shaped before its final shape.
fact: «A plastic bottle is blown from a preform, a small finger-sized plastic tube.»
fact: In design and technology lessons, a preform is heated and blown up inside a mould.
fact: «Perform» means to do something for an audience, such as a play or a song.
fact: In ordinary spelling, preform is often a mistake for perform.
exercise: «A plastic bottle is blown from a preform, a small finger-sized plastic tube.» What is a preform? | A kind of stage show | A mould that holds a bottle | *A partly shaped object, made before its final shape | A drink sold in bottles
exercise: Maya writes «The class will preform a play on Friday.» What word did she probably mean? | *perform | preform | prefer | predict
exercise: In design and technology, what happens to a preform? | It is put on a stage for an audience | *It is heated and blown up inside a mould | It is read aloud to the class | It is thrown away at once
test: What is the best meaning of preform in a design lesson? | *A partly shaped object before its final shape | A plan for a school play | A finished bottle on a shop shelf | A kind of plastic paint
test: Which word means to do a play or a song for an audience? | *perform | preform | prevent | prefix
exam: Ravi reads «The bottle was blown from a preform» and asks, "Does preform mean to do a show?" What should he answer? | *No, a preform is a partly shaped object, so check the clues and the mould | No, it means happy | Yes, it means the same as perform | Yes, because the word looks like perform
